2026-10-08T06:12:04.8335513Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8435576Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8445681Z [0m
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8446445Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8446989Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8447204Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8447697Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8448829Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8449325Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8449791Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8450495Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8450812Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8451641Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8452283Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8452752Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8453099Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8453267Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8453504Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8453757Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8454022Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8454395Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8454523Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8454644Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8454792Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8455352Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8455933Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8458724Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8458848Z I will:
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8458971Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8459255Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8459755Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8460418Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8461314Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8461781Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8462130Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8462909Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-08T06:12:04.8463710Z    /root
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0071565Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0072542Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0090425Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0091464Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0091868Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0092367Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0092757Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0104512Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0105433Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0115977Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0116770Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0117459Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0117671Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0118099Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0118344Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0118613Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0119050Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0119254Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0119360Z If you would like to
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0119639Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0119802Z 
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0120003Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0120347Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-08T06:12:05.0120494Z 
